WEBVTT

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.810
Welcome back, I'm glad you could join me today.

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.090
You ready to do a fantastic little painting with me?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.770
Got your palette all set up and you ready to go?

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:06.330
Good.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.570
Tell you what, let's have them run all the colors

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.250
across the screen that you need to do the painting

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.150
that we're gonna do today.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.570
And they'll come across in exactly the same order

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.590
as I have them on my palette.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.930
Starting with the white, and coming all the way around.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:18.380
And while they're doing that,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.580
let's go on up here and get started.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.510
Now I've already covered the canvas

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.070
with a thin, even coat of liquid white.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.090
It's wet and slick, and it's all ready to go.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.550
So today, let's just have some fun.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:29.750
I'm gonna start out with a small amount of...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.460
Indian yellow, tiniest little bit,

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.900
just tap a little bit onto the brush.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.970
And let's go right up in here in the sky

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:40.440
and just let a little tiny bit of that play around,

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.500
just here and there.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:47.350
Put that in first, just little spots of it,

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:48.700
maybe a little down here.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.080
I'm gonna have a little water in this painting,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.780
so we'll put a little tiny bit right in there.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.450
Then without cleaning the brush,

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.690
I'm gonna go right into a small amount of alizarin crimson.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.190
Just tap the brush.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.520
and leave that Indian yellow in the brush.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:02.500
It makes a pretty color.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:03.960
Okay, let's go back up here.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.210
Now then, I'm just gonna bounce

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.310
a little bit of this crimson here and there.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.740
Just sort of play it around, let it have fun.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.460
Nice warm little sky, happy little sky.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:27.870
Over in here, all kinds of pretty little colors.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:28.830
That looks good enough to eat.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.060
and then we'll put just a touch in the water.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.120
Since we know there's gonna be some water in here,

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.230
just like so.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.180
Okay, now then, without cleaning the brush again,

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.990
I'm gonna go right into a little bit of the midnight black

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.790
and the small amount of phthalo blue.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.880
Blue and black, just a small amount.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.160
This black is so strong.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.280
Okay, let's go back up here.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.040
Now then, in the sky that's remaining,

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.970
it's just sort of down.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.800
dance in a little bit of this blue-black color.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.780
Just let it bounce around and play.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:17.670
Tear in there, wherever you think it oughta be,

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.840
that's exactly where it should be.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.930
Okay, use that same color, blue and black,

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.210
and let's finish up our water area.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:29.960
Now water, unless it's moving,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.560
is always flat, it's level.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.640
So try to keep these strokes as straight as possible,

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.520
it'll make your water look better.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.780
Now very quickly, this blue and black mixture is so strong,

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.690
it'll eat up this little light area,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.950
so try not to cover that up.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.570
We'll save a little touch of that.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.180
That'll be pretty when it's all done.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.410
Okay, let me wash my old brush here.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.860
And if you've painted with me before,

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.390
you know this is the fun part.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.330
Shake it off, and then...

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:02.980
That really is the fun part.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.200
Okay, let's go back up here.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.960
Be sure your brush is clean and dry,

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.620
and I'm gonna very gently,

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:09.610
using little criss-cross patterns,

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.210
just blend all this together.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.710
When you're painting it at home,

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:17.440
you paint as soft as you want it.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.120
The more you blend it, the softer it'll become.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.970
It'll just absolutely all blend together.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.850
There you go.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:29.980
Just let your imagination...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.320
take you wherever you want to be.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:34.650
You know, one of the letters,

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.820
questions I get in letters all the time is,

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.600
where do we get all the ideas

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.840
for the paintings that we do?

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.740
You know, one of the best ways we have

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.000
of coming up with ideas is from cards people send us.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.430
We get cards from fantastic people all over the country,

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.430
and they tell us what they want to see.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.670
A lot of them send, oh, postcards or photographs,

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:56.880
and believe it or not,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.100
that's where the majority of these paintings come from.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.170
Okay, and that quick we have a very colorful, nice little sky.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:06.320
Let's have some fun.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.040
Let's take the old round brush.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.220
I'm gonna go into a little bit of Van Dyke Brown,

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.480
a little bit of the Sienna,

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.220
a touch of Sap Green,

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.020
and we just mix them together on the brush, that brush.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:20.920
Okay, let's go right back up here.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.470
I'm gonna have some happy little bushes back here,

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.380
and I'm just barely tapping the canvas,

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.000
not tapping very hard.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.700
and I want them to get lighter toward the top.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.540
Just make a decision what you think

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.620
your bushes ought to look like, and drop them in.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:41.520
Okay, a little bit more paint.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.910
This is dark sienna, Van Dyke brown,

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:45.990
a little bit of sap green.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:47.940
I don't want too much green.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.440
I want it to stay sort of in the brownish tones.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:58.990
You can take alizarin crimson and sap green

00:04:58.990 --> 00:04:59.970
and mix it together and make a...

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.340
beautiful brown color.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.020
Maybe there's some little things that live right up in here,

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:08.850
just wherever you want.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.020
And if you want to show some things that are far, far away,

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.960
then just barely touch the canvas.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.560
So there's just little tiny indications, see?

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.800
And it looks like little distant, distant things,

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:22.710
far back in the distance.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.100
Barely, barely touching the canvas.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:28.480
Three hairs and some air.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:29.970
Okay, now then.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.580
Let's put a few little highlights on there.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.420
We'll take the same old brush, just leave it dirty.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:37.200
Use a little bit of the yellows, a little green.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.850
Just tap it, see?

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:42.560
Just tap right into it, okay?

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:47.700
Now then, using the top corner of the brush,

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.660
begin laying in a few little basic shapes.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:52.890
And sort of vary the colors

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.430
between all the different yellows.

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:58.150
Barely touching the canvas.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:04.060
Yellow ochre, Indian yellow, cad yellow, all these colors.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.380
And if you have trouble making them stick,

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.840
add the least little touch of the liquid white

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.310
or a little bit of thinner to your brush.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:17.940
Tiniest little bit, tiny little, just enough so it sticks.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.050
There you go.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:28.150
And leave these that are far, far away with nothing on them.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.040
because they're too far away to see any highlights on them.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.270
Don't kill everything with highlights.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:38.580
You'll ruin the illusion of distance in your painting.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:42.720
Hmm, okay.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:47.700
Now then, maybe you want to create the idea of mist

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.140
just floating around here.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.060
Watch right here.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:51.440
Just take the big brush,

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.640
gently tap right on the base of it,

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.320
round the bottom, just tap it.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.760
Avoid taking the brush like this and hitting it.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:02.920
It'll cut it off real straight,

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:04.920
and it looks like somebody took a big knife

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.080
and just cut off all the trees.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.380
You want this line to be very soft and varied.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.620
You don't want a distinct line across there.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.630
You can very lightly, very lightly,

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:16.540
just lift upward a little bit, see?

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.260
And that easy, you have the illusion mist

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:22.500
is floating all down at the bottom of that.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.500
Okay, I'll use the same old dirty brush,

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.800
go right into the browns.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:29.930
This is the Dark Sienna and the Van Dyke.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.610
Let's go right back up here.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:34.030
Maybe there's a happy little hill right here.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.200
Now we don't want to kill all that misty area

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.280
that we put right in here.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.200
That misty area is what separates, what divides.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.840
All we're doing now is putting down a base color

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.820
so our next color will show up.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.820
You need the dark in order for light to show.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:55.270
You knew that.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.400
Alright, while I have this color on my brush,

00:07:59.460 --> 00:07:59.980
I'm gonna pull it.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.220
a tiny bit of it down.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.390
This will create the illusion of a reflection.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:06.920
Straight down, be sure it goes straight down,

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.310
just like that, and then very lightly across,

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:14.940
and it gives you the indication of water.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:15.780
That easy.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.020
Now, same old brush, hadn't cleaned it yet.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.200
Going right into some of the yellows and the green,

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.930
and just tap that brush, see?

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:29.820
Tap it again, all right, come on back up here, and let's.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:32.790
right in here, and drop in some highlights.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.060
Right on top of that dark.

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:39.210
And just like before, if you have problems making it stick,

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.910
add a little bit of the liquid white,

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:42.910
or a little bit of thinner.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.210
Thin paint will stick to a thick paint,

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:52.060
and the base colors that we use are very, very firm.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.350
And here and there, you can even take

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:56.830
a little bit of the red color.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.740
Mm, look at there, pretty.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.460
and just drop in a few little things like that.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:11.480
Put the tiniest amount of thinner on the brush.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.230
See how much easier it sticks?

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.400
Even though my yellows are a little bit thinner

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.400
than the other colors,

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.220
sometimes when you have several layers,

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.920
you want it really thin so it'll stick right up there.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:27.560
Okay, that gives us a nice little background to play with.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:29.910
And if you wanted to, you could even pull it.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.520
a tiny bit of that highlight color

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.720
right down into the reflections, like so.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:37.320
And I'll use another brush, this one's clean,

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.630
and pull it down, this is a clean, dry brush,

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:43.960
and go across, see how it reflects all those colors

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:44.860
right into the reflections?

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:51.010
Alright, let's take the knife,

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.710
and I'll use a little bit of brown here,

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.320
a little bit of the Van Dyke brown.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.620
Pull that paint out as flat as you can get it,

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.960
and then just cut across so you have that little...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.680
a roll of paint right out on the edge of the knife.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:02.460
Okay, let's go up here.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:05.180
Now then, I'm just gonna put,

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.200
just by rubbing it back and forth,

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:10.890
put the indication of a little bit of land back here.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:13.110
Need something for all these little grassy things to set on.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.070
Don't want them to fall off in the water

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:15.990
and make a big splash.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.560
You can take that same brown,

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.360
add a little titanium white to it.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.190
Like that, make a little touch of highlight color,

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.070
just like so.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.160
Okay, I'm gonna take a little of the liquid white,

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:38.460
pull it out very flat, okay, then cut across it.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:39.980
Okay, can you see that?

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:41.930
See, cut across.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.480
That gives you a little tiny roll of paint

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:45.740
right on the knife blade.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:46.400
Let's go up here.

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:48.930
Now then, go straight into the canvas,

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.120
and act like you're trying to saw a hole in it.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.640
Just really get tough with it.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.550
And that cleans up the bottom of your land,

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.080
puts a little water line there.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.370
creates, once again, the illusion of distance in your painting.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.720
Keep these lines basically straight.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.120
You don't want your water to run out on your carpet.

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:14.990
Take a clean knife and just scrape in

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:17.650
the indication of a few little trunks and twigs

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.590
and little things like that here and there.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:22.130
No big deal, wherever you want them.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.500
Okay, time to have some fun here.

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:27.710
Let's go back to our round brush.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:29.970
I'm gonna go right back into the browns.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.250
This is the Dark Sienna, the Van Dyke Brown,

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:36.570
a little bit of the Samp Green we'll throw in there too.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.110
Really tap that brush firmly.

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:40.530
We're gonna get it loaded up.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:42.540
Okay, let's go up here.

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:45.600
Now then, maybe, yep, there is now.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:50.300
Man, we're really, really hitting the canvas quite hard.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.580
You can probably see it bending and hitting it so hard.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:58.490
Let me sock it in there.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.990
Maybe there's a huge, yeah, let's have a big tree

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.600
that lives right here, and he just hangs

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:09.210
right out over like that, look at that,

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:17.600
right on up here, wherever, you make a decision,

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:20.050
wherever you want your tree to live, that's where he lives.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.760
Trees are one of my favorite things to paint,

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:27.630
I think they're so beautiful, okay?

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.400
Let's really get crazy today.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.640
Maybe, yep, maybe there's a happy bush that lives right there.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.000
He's got a friend named Clyde that lives right there.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.730
So you make up little stories when you paint.

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:42.470
It really helps.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:48.070
You don't have to be crazy to do this, but it does help.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:54.270
When you put on your painter's suit,

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.310
you can get away with anything,

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.760
cause everybody thinks us painters, you know,

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:59.220
are a little weird.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:01.790
So we can do anything.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:06.320
And in your painting, you paint things that make you happy.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.830
You create your own visions, your own world.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.220
A lot of the letters that I've received,

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.460
people wanted to know what did I do before I became a painter.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:21.380
I spent half my life in the military.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.740
I worked in the hospital, in the military.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.560
I'd come home from work and I would paint.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:33.690
For over 20 years I would do that.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:36.120
I'd come home and paint because on this canvas,

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:39.180
oh, on this canvas I could have total freedom.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.680
Nobody told me what time to be at work

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:43.200
and what kind of world to make.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.540
Here I could make any kind of world that I wanted.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.740
Any kind of world.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.320
Let's put a big tree right here.

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:53.400
Sometimes I talk too much when I should be painting.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.700
Being in the military for half my life

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.950
allowed me to see parts of the world

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:05.630
that I would have never seen,

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.820
all the way to Southeast Asia and back,

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:13.270
and it introduced me to my favorite place in the world,

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:17.590
Alaska, as some of the most beautiful scenery.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.520
You'll ever get a chance to go there if you haven't been.

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.370
You really should take a trip,

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:27.620
see where a lot of the scenery that I paint comes from,

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.960
and you may be...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:30.840
like me and won't leave.

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:33.310
I just bought a house and stayed there.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:35.580
Okay, there we go.

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:38.730
Well, I've been sitting here talking so much

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.090
I've about covered up the whole canvas,

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:40.770
so why don't we?

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:42.390
Let's just go ahead and fill all this in.

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:46.290
Take it carried away, as I say when I'm talking.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:48.380
Don't know when to stop.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.360
This is still just the dark sienna,

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:59.050
Van Dyke brown, and a little tiny touch of sap green.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:14:59.870
Not much green.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.550
And when you're using a brush this big,

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.850
it doesn't take but a few minutes just to cover it all up.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:11.480
But you can also begin laying in some basic shapes

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.460
and some basic ideas.

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:14.100
You can see them all in here.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.350
And at this point, you're not committed

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.710
because you could put this part on.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.510
Well, in all honesty, you could put it on with a paint roller.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:26.350
Might have a whole new way of painting if it did that.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:32.460
Okay, now you can sort of look at the shape

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:33.280
of some of these trees.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:35.680
I'm gonna, I think I'll make this one a little bigger.

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.580
Shoot, we've covered up most of the canvas already.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:38.860
Why not just keep going with it?

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.000
Beautiful background we worked so hard on,

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:45.980
we just covered it up.

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:49.970
Take an old fan brush,

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:53.890
and I'm gonna go right in Van Dyke Brown.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:57.520
Load that brush full of paint, both sides.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:58.560
Okay, now watch.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:15:59.510
I'm gonna take,

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.520
one side, and go through white, see?

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:05.750
Through both sides with Van Dyke brown,

00:16:05.890 --> 00:16:07.010
and then one side with white.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.520
So I've got white on one side, brown on the other.

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:11.650
There we go, let's go up here.

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:15.560
Now then, let's take it right here,

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:18.110
touch, and give it a little pull.

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:20.760
And by double loading the brush,

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:23.890
we have both sides of the tree trunk at one time.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:25.790
Sneaky, huh?

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:28.740
Isn't that pretty?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:33.510
and it's easy to do, fun to do.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.920
Can't tell you what, let's put a trunk right here

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:38.340
in this old tree, we can't have him

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:40.110
without a nice, strong trunk.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.240
And when you're doing these trunks,

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:45.260
all trees don't become telephone poles,

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:47.480
so make some of them little crooks and bends,

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:49.780
and it makes your painting more interesting.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:54.840
Put little, little, little bends in it,

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:57.450
really, really will brighten up your painting,

00:16:58.340 --> 00:16:59.340
make it look more natural.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.270
Spend some time looking at trees.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.230
I go out in the woods and I hunt with a camera.

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:09.460
Well, I just shoot them dead with a camera.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.350
And then you save these photographs,

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:16.180
and you can take a tree out of one photograph

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:19.530
and maybe put it with another photograph

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:20.590
that has a beautiful sky.

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:21.810
You can combine these things.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.220
Okay, I'm gonna take a little bit of paint thinner

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:27.000
and go right into some bright red.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.580
Right on the liner brush, just turn it.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.160
Okay, let's go right back up here.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:36.630
Maybe on this tree, a little bit of this red

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.210
and just come right down the edge.

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:42.710
Zoop, now very gently, just blend that out.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:46.840
See, doesn't that make a pretty little tree?

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:56.840
It's easy, inside of this one, just blend it out.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:02.140
And if you wanted to, you could add a little bit over in here,

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:06.480
just here and there, wherever you want it, wherever you want it.

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:11.060
Sometimes you can take just a little bit of the liquid white.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:12.400
Let's do it a little different here.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.560
You can take a little liquid white

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.320
and come right down the side and then blend it in

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.920
so it's bright on that far edge

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:20.700
and softer as it goes toward the center of the trunk.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:25.480
Gives you the indication of roundness in your tree trunk.

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:29.800
You can just blend it to whatever degree of softness that you want.

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:34.190
That easy, or you can just take plain liquid white,

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:37.590
and here and there, put an old white trunk.

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:40.130
You know, there's trees that have white bark on them,

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:43.330
and they're pretty, everything's pretty.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:46.900
Happy little tree, there we go.

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:52.780
Now then, a little bit of the liquid black

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:56.080
on the liner brush, and let's make the indication

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:58.550
of a little branch here and there.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:01.800
Just here and there.

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:08.580
This is just straight liquid black there, little things.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:11.860
Okay, that gives you an idea how to do that.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:15.240
Now, I'll get the old round brush.

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:18.950
I'm gonna add a little bit of the liquid white to it.

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:22.060
This is the same old dirty brush,

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:24.080
because I want the colors to be soft and muted,

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:27.030
so I've left all the browns on there.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:28.950
I'm going right into the yellows now.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.430
and I added a small amount of the liquid white

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:33.370
just to thin the paint.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:34.430
Okay, let's go back up here.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:36.500
Now then, let's make some decisions

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:41.080
using just the top of the brush, just the top,

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:41.840
and just touch.

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:43.880
Try not to hit the same area over and over,

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.820
or pretty soon, you'll become a mud mixer,

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:49.220
and if you've painted before,

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:53.640
you've all experienced a little bit of mud mixing.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:55.570
Try to avoid that.

00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:59.530
Here, just worry about some basic shapes.

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:01.320
Barely tapping.

00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:09.320
Don't have to hit hard, don't have to hit him hard.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:14.650
Just enough to get the paint to come off the brush.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.420
Isn't that a super nice, easy way to put all those

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:20.780
little leaves and stuff on the tree?

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.880
Add a little bit of the bright red to that.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.040
Don't get crazy, I'm still just tapping.

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:34.640
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:37.900
Maybe these over here, maybe old Jack Frost

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:38.980
has touched them a little bit.

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:43.130
Beginnin' to see a little color.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:48.240
And this is your creation, so whatever color

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:48.980
you want them to be.

00:20:52.970 --> 00:20:55.010
Once again, remember your little patterns in here.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.910
Don't just throw this on at random.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:20:59.340
Think like a tree.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:01.240
Look like a tree.

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:12.310
Work on these little patterns.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.240
Create all kinds of happy little things in here.

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:19.580
And don't kill all the darks, you need those darks.

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:24.270
Okay, let's go to this other tree.

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:25.890
There's one on the far right.

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:28.410
Don't want him to feel left out.

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.930
We'll give him a few happy little leaves.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:34.680
up here, that's a nice one, that one really worked nice.

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:38.000
When you paint sometimes a brush just hits right

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:41.240
and things, oh they sparkle, they sparkle.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:46.340
That's one of our happy accidents, like those.

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:52.110
I used to spend weeks with a one-haired brush

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:56.350
trying to do all this, lazy.

00:21:58.340 --> 00:21:59.580
Okay, okay.

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:04.230
Let's take, oh, I see another bush right here.

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:06.730
Now you can begin just picking out little individuals.

00:22:08.190 --> 00:22:14.560
Just pick them out and go wherever, wherever you want.

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:17.710
There's one that's got, looks like little flowers on it.

00:22:19.620 --> 00:22:21.620
I'll tell you what, yeah, you want.

00:22:22.190 --> 00:22:24.750
Let's take the fan brush, and it has brown on it still.

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:27.240
I want a happy little path.

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:28.610
It's right back in here.

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:29.970
You'd have to have a way.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.050
of getting back in here and catching that big trout

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.370
that lives right over in there.

00:22:34.570 --> 00:22:36.250
So we'll just put some brown on first,

00:22:37.430 --> 00:22:39.050
then I'll just use the same old dirty brush.

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:41.010
I'll take some dark sienna and some white,

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:44.420
just mix it loosely on the brush,

00:22:46.700 --> 00:22:47.940
barely touching the canvas,

00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:49.680
just let it sort of graze across there.

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:52.560
Wiggle it, make it look like little stones.

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:56.800
This isn't a big paved highway here,

00:22:56.920 --> 00:22:58.400
this has got little stones and rocks,

00:22:58.520 --> 00:22:59.660
so it's not real even.

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:03.540
Just let it disappear right on into the background.

00:23:03.920 --> 00:23:04.460
Like so.

00:23:06.090 --> 00:23:07.310
Okay, let's have some fun.

00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:09.180
And we'll take the two inch brush

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:10.660
and go right into the same colors

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.180
that I've been using, the yellows.

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:14.740
It's all the yellows, all the reds.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:17.370
Just bring them together.

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:21.480
Let's begin making the indication

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:22.900
of little grassy things that are growing

00:23:22.900 --> 00:23:23.940
right up to the path here.

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:25.790
Work in layers.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:29.360
Do the area that's the farthest away first.

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:33.740
and work forward, always working forward, forward, forward.

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:37.270
And make little individual things,

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.290
just don't throw them in there at random.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:44.110
See, you could even make your bush right here, just like so.

00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:48.890
Paint all of them, leave some of them dark.

00:23:53.170 --> 00:23:54.730
Add a little more green to that.

00:23:58.250 --> 00:23:59.810
This whole big brush, you can just tap it.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.690
all kinds of beautiful, beautiful little highlights.

00:24:04.120 --> 00:24:08.010
Like so, work in layers.

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:11.420
I can't say that enough, can't say that enough.

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:17.620
And some little hills, isn't that super?

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:20.220
I think where light would strike.

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:22.700
See that light's coming through there

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:24.080
and just zinging here and there?

00:24:25.950 --> 00:24:27.770
If you think light's really gonna strike here,

00:24:27.850 --> 00:24:28.830
you can add a little white.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.200
Really make it look like light's just coming right through there.

00:24:34.070 --> 00:24:35.710
Okay, let's go over here on this other side

00:24:36.530 --> 00:24:39.140
and put in some happy little things right there.

00:24:44.670 --> 00:24:46.610
Always paying attention to the lay of the land.

00:24:51.420 --> 00:24:53.720
Here it stands out, makes it look like a little rounded area.

00:24:54.360 --> 00:24:56.860
And that helps push that path all the way back up in there.

00:24:58.410 --> 00:24:59.970
Okay, I'm going back to my old family.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.160
that has the brown on it.

00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:05.160
I tell you what, let's get brave, right here, right here.

00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:07.900
Zoom, there's a big ol' tree.

00:25:09.370 --> 00:25:11.840
And he's got a friend, right there.

00:25:14.600 --> 00:25:15.980
Get lonely, we'll give him a friend.

00:25:16.900 --> 00:25:19.160
See, that helps push the whole path area

00:25:19.160 --> 00:25:20.400
back further into the painting.

00:25:20.480 --> 00:25:22.680
I'm gonna take a little bright red,

00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:24.620
a little white and brown, and mix it together here.

00:25:25.220 --> 00:25:26.580
And let's just put the indication

00:25:26.580 --> 00:25:29.020
of some highlight right here.

00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:35.410
Make this tree stand out and really shine in the sunlight.

00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:42.870
Just put a little highlight on him, wherever you want it.

00:25:45.120 --> 00:25:47.040
We'll use a little bit of the brown on the other side

00:25:47.040 --> 00:25:50.170
just to make it dark, dark, dark over here.

00:25:53.520 --> 00:25:55.360
Sort of makes that tree look round.

00:25:56.960 --> 00:25:59.970
Okay, our liner brush with some of the liquid black.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.470
and that quick, that quick gives us

00:26:04.470 --> 00:26:08.440
some happy little tree limbs, see?

00:26:08.620 --> 00:26:11.090
And as many as you want.

00:26:11.430 --> 00:26:13.640
This is your tree, so you just put them

00:26:13.640 --> 00:26:17.970
where you want them and however many you want to go.

00:26:18.560 --> 00:26:20.720
Now we have an indication of a few branches there.

00:26:21.520 --> 00:26:22.740
Let's take the old big brush,

00:26:23.150 --> 00:26:25.930
we'll go right into some sap green and some of the yellows,

00:26:25.970 --> 00:26:29.000
and let's go right up here.

00:26:30.320 --> 00:26:31.520
and then you can put the indication

00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:37.070
of some nice little leaves that live right out here.

00:26:37.210 --> 00:26:46.440
Just like so, and that's all there is to it.

00:26:49.210 --> 00:26:52.360
Just drop them in, and the old clock on the wall

00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:55.320
tells me it's time to sneak out of here for this week.

00:26:56.980 --> 00:26:59.440
So with that, I think we'll call this painting finished.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:00.980
I look forward to seeing you again.

00:27:01.180 --> 00:27:02.480
Happy painting, God bless.
